        "original_id": "81b91595-9b66-5341-b584-3cc439e5bd69",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Revolt of the Beavers, Old Mother Goose's Rhymes, Mother Goose\n- Organizations: Federal Theater Project\n- People: Oscar Saul, Louis Lantz, Arthur Rackham\n- Places: Adelphi Theatre, New York City, United Kingdom\n- Concepts: Mother Goose, Marxism a la Mother Goose, Christmas pantomime\n\nFacts:\n- Mother Goose is the imaginary author associated with a collection of fairy tales and nursery rhymes often published as \"Old Mother Goose's Rhymes.\"\n- In 1913, Arthur Rackham illustrated \"Old Mother Goose's Rhymes.\"\n- On May 20, 1937, the Federal Theater Project staged the children's play \"Revolt of the Beavers\" by Oscar Saul and Louis Lantz at the Adelphi Theatre in New York City.\n- One critic described \"Revolt of the Beavers\" as \"Marxism a la Mother Goose.\"\n- \"Revolt of the Beavers\" ran at the Adelphi Theatre in New York City until June 19, 1937.\n- A Christmas pantomime called \"Mother Goose\" is often performed in the United Kingdom.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
